  "instruction": "Review the committed bits.py patch. solve(mask,low,width) returns width bits starting at low, shifted down to bit0. The supported domain is the Cartesian product mask in [0,1,10,21,31] and (low,width) in [(0,0),(0,5),(1,3),(4,1),(5,0)]. Width0 returns0. Determine whether the patch introduces a violation.\nReview only. Do not modify any workspace file, directory, mode or Git metadata. Review the complete candidate against baseline; the finite witness domain below is normative, not a list of expected answers.\n{\"masks\": [0, 1, 10, 21, 31], \"windows\": [[0, 0], [0, 5], [1, 3], [4, 1], [5, 0]]}\n\nRun the frozen visible command `python3 -B verify.py`; do not edit verify.py. Its result is an observation, not the complete task contract. Use the controller-provided record when available and preserve its exact command/execution_state/exit_code/evidence_availability values in response checks. Return a JSON object with status (completed or blocked), findings (array), blockers (array), checks (array of exactly that one four-field check record). For implementation, successful completion has empty findings and blockers. Review findings each have path (workspace-relative POSIX, no ./), symbol (unqualified function), kind (incorrect-result, unexpected-exception or data-loss), and witness {module,function,args} drawn from the declared finite domain. A witness is a data request, never executable code. A finding must be an introduced contract violation: the baseline meets the expectation, the candidate does not. One or more supported consequences can cover the same root cause; duplicate supported findings are neutral, extra unsupported findings fail. A blocker task requires status blocked, no findings, and one blocker {resource,reason}; do not claim a pass. No extra response fields are required. Python3/standard library only. Do not install packages, change permissions or access a network. Preserve arguments to every callable.\n",
  "visible_command": [
    "python3",
    "-B",
    "verify.py"
  ],
